# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        name: "Tempmail Support"
        url: "https://tempmail.lol"
      }
      description: "The Tempmail API provides users with disposable email addresses that can be used for temporary registrations or verifications. It allows users to manage their temporary inboxes, retrieve emails, and perform various email-related operations securely and anonymously."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Production server"
          url: "https://api.tempmail.lol/v2"
        }
      ]
      title: "Tempmail API"
      version: "2.0.0"
      tagline: "Spin up disposable email inboxes and read their messages via a simple HTTP API"
      homepage: "https://tempmail.lol"
      docs_url: "https://tempmail.lol/api"
      about_md: `[Tempmail.lol](https://tempmail.lol) is a disposable email service that lets you generate throwaway inbox addresses and fetch any mail they receive. This SDK targets the v2 HTTP API hosted at \`https://api.tempmail.lol/v2\`.

The API is built around three resources: available **domains**, generated **email** addresses, and the **inbox** of messages received for a given address. Typical use is to create a temporary address, hand it out to a sign-up form, then poll the inbox for the confirmation message.

Official client libraries exist for JavaScript and Python, and community support is available via the project's Discord. Consult the [API documentation](https://tempmail.lol/api) for current request shapes, authentication requirements, and any plan-based limits.`
      entity_desc: {
        domain: "The set of domain names that the service can issue temporary addresses under."
        email: "A disposable email address generated by the API, used as the receive endpoint for incoming mail."
        inbox: "The collection of messages delivered to a disposable address, retrieved via the API for the address and token issued at creation time."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
